{"name":"Flirtatious Flamingo","hex":"#cc22ff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flirtatious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to flirtation.","Having a tendency to flirt often."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flirtatious"},{"term":"flamingo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wading bird of the family Phoenicopteridae of the order Phoenicopteriformes.","A deep pink color tinged with orange, like that of a flamingo."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep pink color tinged with orange, like that of a flamingo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flamingo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flirting","blocks":[{"text":"Flirting, formally known as coquetry, is a form of social communication via body language, verbal expressions, or written language, intended to evoke feelings of playful excitement and potential romantic or sexual interest. Flirting can change in intention as well as intensity, whether it is performed for short-term fun or employed with a longer-term intention of seeking a romantic or sexual relationship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Das_werdenSie_ja_nachher_schon_sehen.jpg/330px-Das_werdenSie_ja_nachher_schon_sehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flirting"},{"title":"Flamingo","blocks":[{"text":"Flamingos or flamingoes are a type of wading bird in the family Phoenicopteridae, which is the only extant family in the order Phoenicopteriformes. There are four flamingo species distributed throughout the Americas, and two species native to Afro-Eurasia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Flamingos_Laguna_Colorada.jpg/330px-Flamingos_Laguna_Colorada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamingo"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikim